WEBVTT\n\n1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
AI agents can carry valid signatures and
still have no authority to act.

2
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.760
Agent Trust Border is a receiver-owned
admission layer that prevents signed metadata

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:15.380
from being mistaken for permission. Here is
the exact problem. A deploy agent presents

4
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:21.540
an identity. a valid signature. and a declared
capability. But no trusted operation grant

5
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.580
is present. The border keeps integrity.
identity. authority. evidence.

6
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.980
and world truth separate. The result is
UNKNOWN. not approval. Nothing executes.

7
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.780
The receiver creates a challenge bound to the
request. nonce. policy. mapping.

8
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:41.640
and trust profile. Now supply a trusted
one-use grant for deploy on sandbox demo.

9
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:47.340
The same request becomes ADMIT. Effective
scope is only the intersection of request.

10
00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:52.860
grant. and receiver policy: sandbox demo.
one run. Change the target to production.

11
00:00:53.260 --> 00:01:00.460
and the decision becomes DENY: scope exceeded.
Replay the consumed grant.

12
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:09.320
and it is denied again: replay detected. Each
outcome creates a D-S-S-E and Ed25519-signed

13
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:15.680
BorderReceipt. It binds the request. policy.
mapping. reason codes. and effective scope.

14
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.980
and action_executed:false. A separate verifier
recomputes those bindings offline.

15
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:25.280
This is the current evidence explorer. It
replays committed artifacts from the Python

16
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.340
kernel; it does not fake a live action.
Twenty-five tests pass.

17
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:35.540
including twenty named security cases repeated
one hundred times from fresh state:

18
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:40.940
two thousand deterministic executions. This is
a falsifiable Stage One prototype.

19
00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:46.140
not a production gateway. Its source adapter
and identities are synthetic.

20
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.880
It claims neither live protocol conformance.
world truth. benign intent.

21
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.640
nor production security. No model. network.
tool. or requested action runs

22
00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:01.280
inside the trusted path. Agent Trust Border
makes missing authority visible

23
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.760
before an autonomous agent crosses the line.
